<div class="wrap">

  <header class="top">
    <p class="eyebrow">Capabilities &amp; Usage Handbook</p>
    <h1>Cosine, end to end</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">Every knob, what it does, and what to reach for it to
      get a sound. <b>One closed-form equation per note</b> instead of a wavetable
      or a bank of oscillators — a clean, exactly band-limited additive tone, plus
      everything you'd dirty it with afterwards. This page is the reference:
      parameters, worked recipes, the full MIDI map, editor shortcuts, tuning
      workflows, and where the same DSP runs beyond a DAW.</p>

    <div class="facts">
      <div class="fact"><p class="k">Formats</p><p class="v">VST3 · CLAP</p></div>
      <div class="fact"><p class="k">Voices</p><p class="v">24 · stereo</p></div>
      <div class="fact"><p class="k">Parameters</p><p class="v">39</p></div>
      <div class="fact"><p class="k">Presets</p><p class="v">22</p></div>
      <div class="fact"><p class="k">Latency</p><p class="v">0 · 16 in HQ</p></div>
      <div class="fact"><p class="k">Also runs on</p><p class="v">ARM · MCU · wasm</p></div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout teal">
      <span class="lbl">Core &amp; Studio — one binary</span>
      Cosine ships as a free <b>Core</b> tier and a paid <b>Studio</b> tier in the
      same download. <b>Core</b>: the Geometric oscillator, Brightness, Partials,
      Saw / Triangle, the amp envelope, the full multimode filter, unison, pitch
      bend, 12-TET, plus A/B morph, seed codes and the preset bank.
      <b>Studio</b> adds Formant, Character, FM + feedback, the filter envelope,
      the LFO matrix, MPE / per-note expression, HQ mode, and any tuning beyond
      12-TET (microtuning + Scala import). Studio unlocks with a personal
      watermarked key file, verified offline — no dongle, no server. Studio-only
      controls are marked <b>(Studio)</b> below; in Core they're greyed and a
      Studio preset simply sounds like its Core version.
    </div>
  </header>

